he function fn into the slot id of the type object at a (its sub-struct's field when the type"] [225 1 "// has that sub-struct)."] [238 1 "// loadSlot reads the slot id of the type object at a (0: none, or no sub-struct)."] [251 1 "// ---- mirrors ----"] [253 1 "// mirror is the CPython layout of a tuple, list, bytes, float, int or str in the world's memory, a handle's."] [255 17 "// 't' tuple, 'l' list, 'b' bytes, 'f' float, 'i' int, 'u' str"] [256 17 "// the pyi object (a subclass's instance too: its built-in part is mirrored)"] [257 17 "// a tuple's or list's slots as last synchronized"] [258 17 "// a bytes' contents as last synchronized"] [259 17 "// the synchronization epoch of the last copy from C"] [260 2 "// a str's (queue 270, capi_unicode.go): its kind, ASCII flag and characters' address; a str PyUnicode_New made"] [261 2 "// (fresh) keeps a copy of its characters to see what C writes"] [270 2 "// held are the references mirrors hold on their items' handles because Go put the item there (a reference C"] [271 2 "// wrote into a slot is C's own): \"C holds the only reference\" (a brand-new object) is a count less these of 1"] [274 28 "// the mirrors a native (or a closure) used: synchronized to C when it returns"] [278 1 "// mirrorKind is the layout o's handle mirrors (0: a proxy's head only) and the bytes it needs."] [292 19 "// PyByteArrayObject (queue 270: PyByteArray_AS_STRING, GET_SIZE)"] [311 3 "// PySetObject (py-capi-1122: PySet_GET_SIZE reads used): fill 16, used 24, mask 32, table 40, hash 48, finger"] [312 3 "// 56, smalltable 64 (8 entries of 16 bytes), weakreflist 192"] [318 1 "// longDigits are an int's absolute value in CPython's 30-bit digits, least significant first (none for 0)."] [330 1 "// writeLong writes an int's PyLongObject fields at a (Include/cpython/longintrepr.h, 3.14: lv_tag is the digits'"] [331 1 "// count shifted by 3 with the sign in the low bits, 0 positive, 1 zero, 2 negative; then the digits)."] [349 1 "// asFloatValue is 