slots) unless C's"] [1039 2 "// the type's own"] [1052 28 "// the base's own __new__ (tp_alloc's allocation through allocObj)"] [1060 2 "// the handle is the C memory"] [1080 2 "// what PyType_Ready writes back"] [1114 2 "// a pyi base's protocol slots C reads in place (Py_TYPE(o)->tp_free, tp_alloc ...)"] [1125 1 "// builtinBaseOf is the nearest type of t's MRO that is neither a C type nor a heap class (the built-in whose"] [1126 1 "// tp_new and tp_init a C type's instance inherits)."] [1136 1 "// callTupleDict calls f with a C call's positional tuple and keywords' dict (NULL: none) after the leading arguments."] [1163 1 "// mirrorTable: the natives of the full API's layouts (queue 269)."] [1190 2 "// tp_new of a pyi type: a C type's instance over a built-in base allocated (bornNew), else the built-in's __new__"] [1239 2 "// tp_dealloc of a pyi type: a C instance's built-in part given back and its memory freed (a pyi object's own"] [1240 2 "// memory is Go's: nothing)"] [1258 2 "// _PyTuple_Resize (Objects/tupleobject.c): *p a tuple only C holds, made newsize long (a new tuple: pyi's are"] [1259 2 "// Go's), the items past the end given back, the new ones NULL"] [1293 2 "// PyState_AddModule: capi_tail.go (modules by index)"] [1294 2 "// PyErr_NewException (Python/errors.c): a class NAME's last part, of base (Exception by default; a tuple of bases"] [1295 2 "// too) and dict, its __module__ NAME's first part"] [1326 2 "// PyObject_CallFunction, PyObject_CallMethod (Objects/call.c): the arguments Py_BuildValue's format makes, a tuple"] [1327 2 "// its items"] [1414 2 "// _PyObject_GC_New (Python/gc.c; the limited API's PyObject_GC_New before 3.8, xxlimited_35's, py-eval-1122): _PyObject_New's"] [1415 2 "// (pyi's collector tracks the object; PyObject_GC_Track and PyObject_GC_Del as before)"] [1438 2 "// PyWeakref_GetRef, PyWeakref_IsDead (Objects/weakrefobject.c) over pyi's references and proxies (PyWeakref_Check:"] [1439 2 "// a ref, a proxy or a callable proxy); 